H4c sector theorem: if every zeta_k = 1/(1-a_k/a) has |arg zeta_k| < pi/(2(s-1))
    then every e_{i-1}(zeta), i<=s, has |arg| < (s-1)*pi/(2(s-1)) = pi/2, so
    Re( sum_i c_i i! e_{i-1}(zeta) ) > 0 and B(alpha) != 0.  s=2 needs only Re zeta>0,
    which the MAX-MODULUS root supplies (|w|<=1, w!=1 => Re 1/(1-w) >= 1/2).
    s=2 m=3: min_k Re(zeta_k) at the max-modulus root = +0.5684  (>= 1/2 as proved)
    s=2 m=5: min_k Re(zeta_k) at the max-modulus root = +0.5565  (>= 1/2 as proved)
    s=2 m=8: min_k Re(zeta_k) at the max-modulus root = +0.5000  (>= 1/2 as proved)

